    },
    {
      "title": "US trade deal will protect all sensitive Indian interests: Piyush Goyal",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/us-trade-deal-will-protect-all-sensitive-indian-interests-piyush-goyal-126102900870_1.html",
      "description": "Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal on Thursday said India's bilateral trade deal with the US would protect all sensitive interests of the country, asserting that people would celebrate the agreement once its details are made public.\nHe said that the opposition parties who are criticising the agreement lack understanding and knowledge about the subject.\n\"The US free trade deal is sometimes sought to be politicised by a few elements... because of lack of understanding and lack of  knowledge. Details are not yet fully out...I do not know what they (opposition parties) criticise.\n\"But I have the courage of conviction to announce boldly that the US trade deal, once details are out, the people of India will celebrate that not a single sensitive interest of our commerce or any stakeholder has been compromised. On the contrary, India will stand at a very strong comparative advantage and trade is about comparative advantage,\" Goyal said here at the ISID-IDRA national conference.\nIn",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-29T10:12:34"
    }
